{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/119819-best-sidereal-combat-ability","id":119819,"title":"Best Sidereal Combat Ability?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-26T10:31:49-07:00","id":119819,"title":"Best Sidereal Combat Ability?","content":"Besides MA (and Firearms!), what is the Sidereals' most effective combat ability covering the widest range of situations and opponents, assuming they have all the Charms, and cool artifacts/specialties/etc to give them the full benefits? IOW, when the Sid Circle is surrounded by monstrous enemies, unable to escape, and without allies or help, who lasts the longest: The swordsman? The Archer? The...Thrower (Is there a better word for this? &quot;Tosser&quot;? Hm...)? <br /> <br /> Also, is the Sidereal combatant better off with a Soak-based build or a Dodge-based one? And if selecting Caste purely for mech effect, which is better in the long run, Battles or Endings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T11:02:29-07:00","id":119836,"title":"","content":"Swordsmen is the weakest because every (or almost every) melee charm can be combined with every other combat ability. Throw is strong and yet it's cap charm is extremely impractical. Archery would be the best route because you could combine it with melee and it has growth in the form of it's capcharm.<br /> <br /> Dodge is a better alternative to soak as a ranged combatant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-26-2014, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T11:11:37-07:00","id":119839,"title":"","content":"Thematically, I like Sidereal Thrown the best, the Gull's trapping is about a funny hobo enjoying each day while the Sutra and the charms are all about pain, suffering, downward-spiral and hopelessness. And the image of the opponent being continuously swarm by a bunch of flying panties is too hilarious. Sidereal Melee is about control the battlefield and the flow of combat, but since most of the charms is just reskin from Solar-Melee/Malfeas Charms so it become the least interesting Ability for me. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T12:13:53-07:00","id":119882,"title":"","content":"Melee has the unique advantage of synergizing with all combat abilities, as well as the more reliable of the two Sidereal perfect defenses. Archery has ridiculous damage potential thanks to Every Direction Arrow, and the prayer strip Charm grants it versatility unparalleled in the entirety of the Sidereal Charmset. Since both are Battles abilities, and since Athletics and Presence are both quite good, I'd give the primacy to Shieldbearers over Reckoners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T12:52:02-07:00","id":119904,"title":"","content":"Definitely love for the versatility of Archery. You can have an arrow for virtually every situation. Or snatch a fish out of the water and use it as an arrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T15:33:11-07:00","id":119998,"title":"","content":"Dodge is generally better than Resistance for fighting any combat-ready Exalt, but there are good reasons to favor the latter. The first thing I'll say about Dodge is that you really need Performance to make it work well and get a high DDV, so at that point you're as well-off playing a Joybringer as you are a Shieldbearer anyway. As a side note, you'll need MA anyway for a flurrybreaker.<br /> <br /> Sidereal Resistance is actually an extremely powerful tree, but it gets overlooked because having a high PDV or DDV is more important in the game of who-can-one-hit-the-other-first. It doesn't enhance armor well, but it does make hitting the Sidereal a dangerous and expensive proposition, and that can have the interesting effect of making you a secondary target.<br /> <br /> Offensively- well, people have already talked about how Sidereal Melee is actually just a tree which enhances all other combat trees, so that's that. Sidereal Archery is a very, very nice sniping tree and the most versatile of all the Sidereal trees- but it has one major weakness. The capstone charm which allows you to seriously change things up and increases your range and all that jazz? It's stationary. You can't take advantage of the traditional benefit of Exalted's long-range archery, which is kiting. That means that Sidereal Archery is an incredibly powerful support offense, but is ideally something you start once the enemies are all engaged.<br /> <br /> Sidereal Thrown, on the other hand, is great for both kiting and for chasing people running from you. It's also got a very nice use in combination with Sidereal Resistance- if you've got both Optimistic Security Practice and Pain Amplification Stratagem on, you'll drain WP both by attacking and through being attacked. Combined with Shield of Destiny and Unrelenting Torment Technique, you get a very dangerous build, both to yourself and to others.<br /> <br /> Sadly, none of this measures up to MA, but there are certainly good characters to be made therein.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T16:40:16-07:00","id":120024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/119819-best-sidereal-combat-ability?p=119998#post119998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Offensively- well, people have already talked about how Sidereal Melee is actually just a tree which enhances all other combat trees, so that's that. Sidereal Archery is a very, very nice sniping tree and the most versatile of all the Sidereal trees- but it has one major weakness. The capstone charm which allows you to seriously change things up and increases your range and all that jazz? It's stationary. You can't take advantage of the traditional benefit of Exalted's long-range archery, which is kiting. That means that Sidereal Archery is an incredibly powerful support offense, but is ideally something you start once the enemies are all engaged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless it's in the errata there's nothing that says it's stationary. The strip is above the sidereal's bow but other than pretty much negating stealth it doesn't say you have to stay in place.<br /> <br /> Also, the only reason MA is the best is just because you get SMA. Archery is honestly better than MA until you get far enough to be able acquire SMA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T16:48:22-07:00","id":120026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/119819-best-sidereal-combat-ability?p=120024#post120024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless it's in the errata there's nothing that says it's stationary. The strip is above the sidereal's bow but other than pretty much negating stealth it doesn't say you have to stay in place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, it looks like I was mistaken. I wonder what I was thinking of? Well, ignore that whole bit, then.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the fact of the matter is that Archery is the best combat style for pretty much everybody anywho.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T18:26:10-07:00","id":120073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/119819-best-sidereal-combat-ability?p=120026#post120026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, the fact of the matter is that Archery is the best combat style for pretty much everybody anywho.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Archery would be one of the best trees ever even if Generalized Ammunition Technique was the only Charm in the tree. <br /> <br /> Entertaining things to fire: Porcupines, asparagus, underwear, trees, harmony (harmony oh love), apples, prayer strips, an argument","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T09:31:08-07:00","id":120381,"title":"","content":"Since the healing option in Many Missiles Bow Technique got nerf by errata, I wonder if Battle Medic is still a viable combat healer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}